/*****************************************************************************
    jitJ7 -- RUNG 7 OF THE jitLadder. 2026-07-31.
    J6 + THE FALLBACK COLUMN MEETING A REAL opMethod.

    J6 emitted a call to a purpose-built helper. J7 emits a call to an EXISTING
    OPERATOR -- opRem, one of the 24 ungated ops -- and UNBOXES ITS RETURN VALUE
    back into the emitted code. That is the complete calling story:
    EMIT A CALL, GET A VALUE BACK, LAYOUT-FREE ON BOTH LEGS.

        jgOut = jgIn % 3;

        fire 1   jgIn = 17  ->  jgOut = 2
        fire 2   jgIn = 19  ->  jgOut = 1      NO RECOMPILE

    ⚠ THE INPUTS ARE CHOSEN SO THE ANSWERS DIFFER, and remainder is the first
    construct where that takes care. 17 % 3 and 20 % 3 are BOTH 2 -- a two-fire
    rung on that pair would pass with a folded constant and prove nothing. 19
    lands on a different remainder, so (2, 1) can only come from arithmetic
    performed at run time on the live field.
    THE GENERAL RULE THIS ADDS TO RUNG STYLE: it is not enough for the two
    inputs to differ; THE TWO ANSWERS MUST DIFFER. Every earlier rung got that
    for free because its operation was injective over the inputs used.

    ⚠ AND THE ARITY REFINES J6. runOP has TWO calling conventions:
        op.isOperator ->  operat(arg,target)   TWO-arg   <- `%` is this
        op.isMethod   ->  method(target)       ONE-arg   <- J6's trace was this
    `'%' operateMethod=opRem` makes it an operator. J6's "the ground agrees,
    one-argument" was true OF THE isMethod ARM ONLY. The fallback column is
    mostly binary operators, so it is mostly two-arg -- which is what the
    ruling's SIGNATURE-KIND TABLE COLUMN is for.

    BOTH LEGS ARE LAYOUT-FREE: the call hands back a GroupItem*, and
    jitUnboxCount -- a helper CALL, never GEP arithmetic -- turns it into an
    i32. Baked struct offsets would break silently on any GroupBody layout
    change, in emitted code, with no compiler to catch it.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (standing harness rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitLadder7);
define
    jgIn;
    jgOut;
    jitJ7 code={ jgOut = jgIn % 3; };
    ;

jgIn  = 17;
jgOut = 0;
print "J7 fire 1 setup : jgIn =" jgIn:;
testing(jitJ7);
print "J7 fire 1 result: jgOut =" jgOut " (want 2)":;

jgIn  = 19;
jgOut = 0;
print "J7 fire 2 setup : jgIn =" jgIn " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "J7 fire 2 result: jgOut =" jgOut " (want 1; 2 = FOLDED at compile time)":;

jgIn  = 17;
jgOut = 0;
jitJ7();
print "J7 interpreted  : jgOut =" jgOut " (the oracle -- want 2)":;

print "J7 SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
